    "reason": "The assertion that the retrieval step and injection step together constitute the mechanism for RAG is valid based on general knowledge. General explanatory knowledge confirms that Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) functionally relies on a two-stage pipeline: first, fetching relevant context from an external corpus (retrieval), and second, integrating that context into the model's input stream (injection). This combined process directly addresses the explanatory gap regarding 'how' external documents are utilized by the transformer. The source text establishes the capability to use external documents but omits the specific integration mechanism; this claim fills that gap without contradicting the source, as it describes the standard operational definition of RAG rather than asserting a specific unverified implementation detail for this particular case.",
